        "id": 1152319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-09-30T23:25:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "do we need this check? we can only get to this point if either (1) total_read_count \u003d\u003d 0 or (2) total_read_count !\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 state-\u003etotal_write_count \u003c\u003d START_PAYLOAD_SIZE. \n\nin case (1), if we don\u0027t do this guard, we\u0027ll get this_read_count \u003d 0, last_sub_transaction \u003d true (but last_sub_transaction only affects what happens for reads).\n\nin case (2), the condition is satisfied except for the case of state-\u003etotal_write_count \u003d\u003d START_PAYLOAD_SIZE. what is special about being exactly equal to START_PAYLOAD_SIZE? and shouldn\u0027t we still make sure that this_read_count is under read_limit in such case?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 626,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 626,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "0dc5e657759e133fc521617135f8c4c41b35280b",
