      "writtenOn": "2021-10-01T23:52:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, looks like now the logic is correct.\n\nI still feel it deserves the refactoring I mentioned above. it may even result in a smaller code since on one hand we add an extra check (and possibly function call, though likely the compiler will inline it since it\u0027s the only place where process_write_read_request() and process_pure_write_request() will be used), but on the other we remove multiple ifs along the way (when we decide if it\u0027s possible that it is a last transaction or check if we total_read_count was \u003e 0 and we need to shared_mem_release(). so, the results should be at least close (if not better in a separate case) both in code size and performance. but the difference in readability will be significant.\n\nbut I\u0027m ok to land this as-is and consider the refactoring separately.",
